 Falling prices are a reflection of weak demand and tight credit conditions that reduce the number of potential buyers Purchasing stays low," says Stan Humphries, chief economist at Zillow Of the nearly 131 million housing units in this country, 112.5 million are occupied 38 million are rented, but that's up by over a million year over year Now to vacancies There were 18.4 million vacant homes in the U.S. in Q4 '10 (11 percent of all housing units vacant all year round), which is actually an improvement of 427,000 from a year ago, but not for the reasons you'd think Vacancies in the apartment sector have been falling steadily and dramatically, why

